          "maintenance": false,
          "text": "“ Permitted Junior Lien Term Loan Debt ” means Debt in the form of junior lien secured term loans or junior lien debt securities (whether registered or privately placed) incurred by the Parent, the Borrower and/or Finance Co; provided that (a) after giving Pro Forma Effect to the incurrence of such Debt (and the use of proceeds thereof), the Secured Leverage Ratio shall not exceed 2.00 to 1.00, (b) at the time of and"
        },
        {
          "type": "leverage",
          "limit": 3.0,
          "unit": "x",
          "direction": "min",
          "maintenance": false,
          "text": "“ Specified Conditions ” means, as of any date, that: (a) no Default, Event of Default or Borrowing Base Deficiency has occurred and is continuing; (b) the Total Revolving Credit Exposures is not greater than eighty percent (80%) of the Total Revolving Commitments and (c) the Leverage Ratio is equal to or less than 3.00 to 1.00 on a Pro Forma Basis."
        }
